     Overlays that have to be compiled into the target APK rather than shipped
     as a runtime resource overlay. Excluded from PRODUCT_ENFORCE_RRO_TARGETS
     in device.mk; see the comment there.
-->
<resources>
    <!-- RegulatoryInfoDisplayActivity is declared with
             android:enabled="@bool/config_show_regulatory_info"
         and manifest attributes are resolved from the APK's own resources when
         the package is parsed, so an RRO cannot reach them.

         RegulatoryInfoOverlayCypfr sets this bool and supplies the image, but
         being an RRO it only takes effect at runtime: the About phone entry
         appeared (RegulatoryInfoPreferenceController reads the bool live) while
         the activity itself stayed disabled, so tapping it did nothing.

             am start -a android.settings.SHOW_REGULATORY_INFO
               Error: Activity class {com.android.settings/...
               RegulatoryInfoDisplayActivity} does not exist.

         Baking it in here enables the component at parse time. The RRO still
         provides the drawable. -->
    <bool name="config_show_regulatory_info">true</bool>
</resources>
